From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:10:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Evict shaped text far from the viewport and rebuild a root
 whose style changes it

Inline roots far from the viewport keep their shaped text, which is most of a long document's
retained layout. Keep a break summary for each root and release the shaped lines, replaying them
from the summary when a root comes back into view. Each scan decides per resident root whether to
keep it, spare it because it was read since the last scan, or evict it.

A root evicted that way keeps the summary it took under the style of the time, and only RELAYOUT
damage reached it when the style changed how text breaks, so it laid out from the old summary while
its rebuilt text took the new style. Compare the wrap mode and tab size too, and an inline span's
padding, border and radius, which parley bakes into line breaking when the layout is built. Either
sends the rebuild path ALL_DAMAGE. The background brush is left out of the decoration comparison
because stylo.rs already handles a change in background presence.
